{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q138657609","formula":"C₆H₁₀N₂O₄","hill":"C6H10N2O4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":10.0,"N":2.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Ribose aminooxazoline"},"descriptions":{"en":"Ribose aminooxazoline (RAO) is a bicyclic pentose aminooxazoline that plays a central role in the prebiotic synthesis of RNA. RAO is a key intermediate in the cyanosulfidic synthesis pathway leading to the prebiotic formation of canonical pyrimidine ribonucleosides. The formation of RAO within the cyanosulfidic reaction network bypasses an otherwise improbable formation of N-glycosidic bonds between nucleobases and ribose sugars. RAO possesses low solubility in comparison to other pentose aminooxazolines, forming chemically stable RAO crystals capable of undergoing chiral enrichment under ambient conditions."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":10888406,"mass":174.15,"charge":0,"smiles":"C([C@@H]1[C@H]([C@@H]2[C@H](O1)N=C(O2)N)O)O","inchikey":"IVFVSTOFYHUJRU-AIHAYLRMSA-N","iupac":"(3aS,5R,6R,6aR)-2-amino-5-(hydroxymethyl)-3a,5,6,6a-tetrahydrofuro[2,3-d][1,3]oxazol-6-ol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"10888406","atoms":22,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.747,"y":-1.127,"z":0.52,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.502,"y":0.878,"z":-0.293,"el":"O"},{"x":0.849,"y":2.355,"z":-0.322,"el":"O"},{"x":3.219,"y":-1.317,"z":-0.858,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.721,"y":-1.269,"z":0.448,"el":"N"},{"x":-3.216,"y":-0.346,"z":-1.177,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.631,"y":0.793,"z":0.828,"el":"C"},{"x":0.783,"y":1.208,"z":0.495,"el":"C"},{"x":1.317,"y":-0.027,"z":-0.206,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.519,"y":-0.7,"z":1.074,"el":"C"},{"x":2.831,"y":-0.128,"z":-0.189,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.157,"y":-0.319,"z":-0.32,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.073,"y":1.361,"z":1.653,"el":"H"},{"x":1.341,"y":1.391,"z":1.422,"el":"H"},{"x":0.958,"y":-